{"title":"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For every positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/6/4e66db1ce558cf1817f1579286937d4ed44e956b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(n)=\\frac{n}{1 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5 \\cdots (2n+1)}.\\]\" width=\"213\" height=\"37\" /> Suppose that the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/1/df124c49d8bed15e96d979766e3da5a0dc311a22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)+f(2)+\\cdots+f(2020)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"215\" height=\"18\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/7347a1d5586e82c832f61ea799d89945ed2837fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{p}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"11\" height=\"36\" /> for relatively prime integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/1/e91d8048fb5306ee0b1676e1b0d8eb86b0c48379.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n) = f(1)+f(2)+\\cdots+f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"252\" height=\"18\" />. We claim that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/2/842002073f6eaa869ce8cb74a56fbfeba4ea5f61.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S(n) = \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{2 \\cdot (2n+1)!!}.\\]\" width=\"201\" height=\"41\" /> We show this using induction. Suppose this is true for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/f/14f9a7f0a078b361958b8019646cc77aaac7ef78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />. Then, it must be true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f05f085f774fc8ab50676b778b86a1f1d1114fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />. The base case when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00fab47c0b9d0ce398d03e57d6720129d53434f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is trivial. Then, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/b/ccb565aeb78bf7a817d07fded8ea47a953b196f5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} S(k+1) &amp;= f(k+1) + S(k) \\\\ {} &amp;= \\frac{n+1}{(2n+3)!!} + \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{2 \\cdot (2n+1)!!} \\\\ {} &amp;= \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{2 \\cdot (2n+3)!!}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"328\" height=\"115\" /> Hence, this completes the induction therefore proving the claim. So, the numerator <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/8/de8e12b91a351963c0b0fe111b5828407d4b2398.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(4041!! - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"103\" height=\"37\" />. \n</p><p>We proceed using Euler's Theorem combined with Chinese Remainder Theorem. It is obvious that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/0/9802e10b213992e811ecb1cac20f25dce9052025.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4041!! \\equiv 0 \\pmod{125}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"168\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/929ea8a290e598abc318b6ff5b8e8e46e68f06eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\equiv 62\\pmod{125}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />. Also, instead of considering <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we consider it modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Then, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/1/f212b92aba6bfa45e5e9e2a040a0dd8e820b7c3b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4041!! \\equiv 3^{253} \\cdot 5^{253} \\cdot 7^{253} \\cdot 9^{252} \\cdot 11^{252} \\cdot 13^{252} \\cdot 15^{252} \\equiv 3 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 9 \\equiv 1\\pmod{16},\\]\" width=\"540\" height=\"19\" /> by Euler's Totient Theorem as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/4/3f46398bc35cd29ba605983cdfff56727bc4f6a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi(16) = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />. This implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/0/c40d77deef5803605fc99a1f47c5b3f9c5c0c798.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(4041!! - 1) \\equiv 0\\pmod{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"209\" height=\"37\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/6/2a673f85e87e060a3922299fd79c26a9be31815b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\equiv 0\\pmod{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" />. Solving the system of congruences, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/1/261179ff719a43d2bf4b182dbee4ca7b2df4adf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\equiv \\boxed{312}\\pmod{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"170\" height=\"23\" />. \n</p><p>~rocketsri (based off of official solution)\n</p><p>(minor edit/fix by Bigbrain_2009)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I\" title=\"2020 CIME I\">2020 CIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2020 CIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2020\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2020 CIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"CIME Problems and Solutions\"> All CIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:MAC_Notice&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Template:MAC Notice (page does not exist)\">Template:MAC Notice</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018013013\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.044 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 200/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1475/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5053/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   10.208      1 -total\n 70.62%    7.209      1 Template:CIME_box\n 26.03%    2.657      1 Template:MAC_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:19603:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018013013 and revision id 241607. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}